          <h3>Vocal Coaching</h3>
          <p>Lessons combine technical vocal training with body awareness, breathing, movement, imagination, and creative expression. Depending on your needs, we can work on vocal technique, confidence, musicality, performance, vocal freedom, or simply finding more comfort in your own voice.</p>
          <p>Whether you are a beginner discovering your voice for the first time, an experienced singer wishing to refine your skills, or someone who simply loves to sing, the lessons are tailored to your individual goals and pace. Together, we will explore your voice in a healthy, sustainable, and supportive environment, where curiosity, playfulness, and authenticity are just as important as technique.</p>
          <p class="lesson-card__for">The goal is not to become someone else's voice, but to discover your own.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="lesson-card lesson-card--healing">
          <svg class="lesson-card__icon" viewBox="0 0 200 60" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M0,30 C25,10 45,50 70,30 C95,10 115,50 140,30 C165,10 185,50 200,30" />
          </svg>
          <h3>Vocal Exploration</h3>
          <p>This is for those who want a more holistic approach to voice, working with vocal sounding, exploration, and body work to find more comfort in using and expressing your voice freely. In a safe space, inspired by Paul Newham's Voice Movement Therapy — the idea that everything that happens in our life leaves a trace on our voice, and that the voice is also a way out — I combine my own work with sound healing, breathwork, and bodywork to support each client in their own way.</p>
          <p>I want to help you befriend your voice and let it exist in the space.</p>
          <p class="lesson-card__for">For anyone looking for a different way into vocal work — who feels stuck, or is looking for a safe place to express their voice and find comfort through it.</p>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

